ist></back><floats-group><table-wrap id="T1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Sociodemographic Characteristics</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ymj-49-46-i001"/></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T2" position="float"><label>Table 2</label><caption><p>Scores of the SCL-90-R Depression and Somatization Subscales, the Anger Expression Scale and the SSRS in Each of the Psychiatric Patients</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ymj-49-46-i002"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>SCL-90-R, symptom checklist-90-revised; SSRS, somatic stress response scale.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T3" position="float"><label>Table 3</label><caption><p>The Relationship between Anger-in, Anger-out, SCL-90-R Hostility and Depression Subscale Scores with the Level of Organ System Symptoms in Depressive Disorder and Somatoform Disorder Patients</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ymj-49-46-i003"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>The Pearson correlation test was used.</p><p>Results of the statistical analysis were described as Pearson correlation coefficients.</p><p>SSRS, somatic stress response ccale; SCL-90-R, symptom checklist-90-revised; AI, anger-in subscale of anger expression scale; AO, anger-out subscale of anger expression scale.</p><p><sup>*</sup><italic>p</italic> &#x0003c; 0.05.</p><p><sup>&#x02020;</sup><italic>p</italic> &#x0003c; 0.01.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-group></article>